Article 9 The types of administrative compulsory measures include:
(1) Restriction of personal freedom of citizens;
(2) Seizure of premises, facilities, or property;
(3) Impoundment of property;
(4) Freezing of deposits or remittances;
(5) Other administrative compulsory measures.

Article 12 The methods of administrative compulsory enforcement include:
(1) Imposition of an additional fine or late fee;
(2) Transfer of deposits or remittances;
(3) Auction or lawful disposal of seized or impounded premises, facilities, or property;
(4) Removal of obstacles and restoration to the original condition;
(5) Substituted performance;
(6) Other methods of compulsory enforcement.

Article 18 When an administrative organ implements administrative compulsion measures, it shall comply with the following provisions:
(1) Before implementation, a report shall be made to and approval obtained from the person in charge of the administrative organ;
(2) Implementation shall be carried out by two or more administrative law enforcement personnel;
(3) Law enforcement identification documents shall be presented;
(4) The party shall be notified to be present;
(5) The party shall be informed on the spot of the reasons and basis for taking the administrative compulsion measures, as well as the rights and relief channels enjoyed by the party according to law;
(6) The statements and defenses of the party shall be heard;
(7) An on-site record shall be made;
(8) The on-site record shall be signed or sealed by the party and the administrative law enforcement personnel; if the party refuses, this fact shall be noted in the record;
(9) If the party is not present, a witness shall be invited to be present, and the witness and the administrative law enforcement personnel shall sign or seal the on-site record;
(10) Other procedures prescribed by laws and regulations.

Article 20 When implementing administrative compulsion measures restricting the personal freedom of citizens according to law, in addition to fulfilling the procedures prescribed in Article 18 of this Law, the following provisions shall also be complied with:
(1) Notify the family members of the party on the spot or immediately after implementing the administrative compulsion measure of the administrative organ implementing the measure, the location, and the duration;
(2) If an administrative compulsion measure is implemented on the spot in an emergency, immediately after returning to the administrative organ, report to the person in charge of the administrative organ and go through the approval procedures retroactively;
(3) Other procedures prescribed by law.
Implementation of administrative compulsion measures restricting personal freedom shall not exceed the statutory time limit. Where the purpose of implementing the administrative compulsion measure has already been achieved or the conditions have ceased, the measure shall be immediately lifted.

Article 24 Where an administrative organ decides to implement seizure and impoundment, it shall fulfill the procedures prescribed in Article 18 of this Law, and produce and deliver on the spot the written decision on seizure and impoundment and the inventory.
The written decision on seizure and impoundment shall specify the following matters:
(1) The name or designation and address of the party;
(2) The reasons, basis, and duration for the seizure and impoundment;
(3) The names, quantities, etc., of the premises, facilities, or property being sealed up or seized;
(4) The channels and time limits for applying for administrative reconsideration or filing an administrative action;
(5) The name, seal, and date of the administrative organ.
The inventory of seizure and impoundment shall be made in duplicate and kept by the party and the administrative organ respectively.

Article 28 Under any of the following circumstances, the administrative organ shall promptly make a decision to lift the seizure and impoundment:
(1) The party has not committed an illegal act;
(2) The premises, facilities, or property being sealed up or seized are unrelated to the illegal act;
(3) The administrative organ has already made a handling decision on the illegal act and no longer needs to seal up or seize;
(4) The period for seizure and impoundment has already expired;
(5) Other circumstances where the measures of seizure and impoundment are no longer needed.
Upon lifting the seizure and impoundment, the property shall be returned immediately; where fresh goods or other property not easy to keep have been auctioned or sold off, the proceeds from the auction or sale shall be returned. If the sale price is obviously lower than the market price and causes losses to the party, compensation shall be given.

Article 31 Where deposits and remittances are frozen according to law, the administrative organ that made the decision shall deliver a written freeze decision to the party within three days. The written freeze decision shall specify the following matters:
(1) The name or designation and address of the party;
(2) The reasons, basis, and duration for the freeze;
(3) The account number and amount frozen;
(4) The channels and time limits for applying for administrative reconsideration or filing an administrative action;
(5) The name, seal, and date of the administrative organ.

Article 33 Under any of the following circumstances, the administrative organ shall promptly make a decision to lift the freeze:
(1) The party has not committed an illegal act;
(2) The frozen deposits or remittances are unrelated to the illegal act;
(3) The administrative organ has already made a handling decision on the illegal act and no longer needs to freeze;
(4) The freeze period has already expired;
(5) Other circumstances where the freeze measure is no longer needed.
Where the administrative organ makes a decision to lift the freeze, it shall promptly notify the financial institution and the party. Upon receiving the notice, the financial institution shall immediately lift the freeze.
Where the administrative organ fails to make a handling decision or a decision to lift the freeze within the time limit, the financial institution shall lift the freeze as of the date of expiration of the freeze period.

Article 35 Before an administrative organ makes a decision on compulsory enforcement, it shall first urge the party to perform its obligations by a notice of urging. The notice of urging shall be made in writing and shall specify the following matters:
(1) The time limit for performing the obligation;
(2) The manner of performing the obligation;
(3) If it involves payment of money, the specific amount and method of payment shall be stated;
(4) The rights of the party to make statements and to defend themselves as enjoyed according to law.

Article 37 If a party still fails to perform the administrative decision within the prescribed time limit after催告, without justifiable reasons, the administrative organ may make a decision on compulsory enforcement.
The decision on compulsory enforcement shall be made in writing and shall specify the following:
(1) the name or title and address of the party;
(2) the reasons and basis for compulsory enforcement;
(3) the means and time of compulsory enforcement;
(4) the channels and time limit for applying for administrative reconsideration or instituting administrative proceedings; and
(5) the name, seal and date of the administrative organ.
During the period of催告, if there is evidence indicating an intention to transfer or conceal property, the administrative organ may make an immediate decision on compulsory enforcement.

Article 39 Enforcement shall be suspended under any of the following circumstances:
(1) the party has genuine difficulties in performing the administrative decision or temporarily lacks the ability to perform;
(2) a third party claims a right to the subject matter of enforcement, and the claim is well-grounded;
(3) enforcement may cause irreparable loss, and the suspension of enforcement does not harm the public interest; or
(4) other circumstances where the administrative organ deems suspension of enforcement necessary.
After the circumstances causing the suspension of enforcement disappear, the administrative organ shall resume enforcement. If there is no obvious social harm, the party genuinely lacks the ability to perform, and enforcement has been suspended for three full years without being resumed, the administrative organ shall no longer enforce.

Article 40 Enforcement shall be terminated under any of the following circumstances:
(1) a citizen dies, leaving no estate available for enforcement, and there is no person to assume the obligation;
(2) a legal person or other organization is terminated, leaving no property available for enforcement, and there is no person to assume the obligation;
(3) the subject matter of enforcement is lost;
(4) the administrative decision on which enforcement is based is revoked; or
(5) other circumstances where the administrative organ deems termination of enforcement necessary.

Article 51 Vicarious performance shall comply with the following provisions:
(1) a written decision shall be served before vicarious performance, and the decision on vicarious performance shall specify the party's name or title and address, the reasons and basis for vicarious performance, the means and time, the subject matter, the cost estimate, and the person performing vicariously;
(2) three days before vicarious performance, the party shall be urged to perform; if the party performs, the vicarious performance shall be stopped;
(3) during vicarious performance, the administrative organ that made the decision shall send personnel to supervise on site;
(4) after the vicarious performance is completed, the supervising personnel of the administrative organ, the person performing vicariously, and the party or a witness shall sign or seal the enforcement documents.
The cost of vicarious performance shall be reasonably determined based on the actual cost and shall be borne by the party, unless otherwise provided by law.
Vicarious performance shall not involve violence, coercion, or other illegal means.

Article 55 To apply to a People's Court for compulsory enforcement, an administrative organ shall provide the following materials:
(1) A written application for compulsory enforcement;
(2) The written administrative decision, along with the facts, reasons, and basis thereof;
(3) The opinions of the party and the status of the administrative organ's urging;
(4) Information on the subject matter of the requested compulsory enforcement;
(5) Other materials as prescribed by laws and administrative regulations.
The written application for compulsory enforcement shall be signed by the responsible person of the administrative organ, affixed with the seal of the administrative organ, and dated.

Article 61 Where an administrative organ, in implementing administrative compulsion, commits any of the following acts, the administrative organ at the next higher level or the relevant department shall order it to make corrections, and the persons directly in charge and the other persons directly responsible shall be given sanctions according to law:
(1) the act has no basis in laws or regulations;
(2) the subject, conditions or manner of administrative compulsion is altered;
(3) the administrative compulsion is implemented in violation of statutory procedures;
(4) administrative compulsory enforcement is implemented at night or on statutory holidays in violation of the provisions of this Law;
(5) the residents are forced to perform relevant administrative decisions by means of cutting off water, electricity, gas supply, heat supply, etc.; or
(6) other circumstances in which the administrative compulsion is illegally implemented.

Article 62 Where an administrative organ, in violation of the provisions of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the administrative organ at the next higher level or the relevant department shall order it to make corrections, and the persons directly in charge and the other persons directly responsible shall be given sanctions according to law:
(1) the scope of sealing up, seizure or freezing is expanded;
(2) the sealed-up or seized premises, facilities or property are used or damaged;
(3) no decision on disposition is made within the statutory period for sealing up or seizure, or the sealing up or seizure is not released in a timely manner according to law; or
(4) no decision on disposition is made within the statutory period for freezing deposits or remittances, or the freezing is not released in a timely manner according to law.

Article 65 Where a financial institution, in violation of the provisions of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the financial regulatory authority shall order it to make corrections, and the persons directly in charge and the other persons directly responsible shall be given sanctions according to law:
(1) disclosing information to a party before freezing;
(2) failing to freeze or transfer the deposits or remittances that should be frozen or transferred immediately, thereby causing the deposits or remittances to be transferred;
(3) freezing or transferring the deposits or remittances that should not be frozen or transferred; or
(4) failing to release the freeze on deposits or remittances in a timely manner.
